scene: The council will give the centre a year's grant on one condition: every group pays for its room. The pensioners' tea and the Friday youth night have always met for free.
scene W: {N} took the post on one promise: the door is open to everyone, whatever they can pay.
scene U: {N} has the room bookings for the year in front of them: the paying groups already cover the heating, nearly.
scene B: Without the grant the boiler is not replaced, and {Ns} own post is cut to three days a week.
scene R: The youth night heard already, and one of the kids asked {N} straight out whether they are being thrown out.
scene G: The pensioners' tea has met every Tuesday since the hall was built, and some of them carried its first bricks.
- W | take the grant and keep one free room for anyone who cannot pay | v: universalism, benevolence | sphere: gather.W | chance: 75
- U | show the council the bookings and ask for a lower, fairer charge | v: achievement, universalism | sphere: gather.U | chance: 75
